    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Tyler Freeman** anchor our lineup as the highest-projected options. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a massive SP_xERA edge (5.41) against Aldegheri, receiving a 19% efficiency boost from the favorable matchup. Meanwhile, **Tyler Freeman** stands as an elite play (71.09) thanks to an anticipated #2 spot in the order and a strong combination of park factors and pitcher vulnerability. Both players are critical for us today, particularly as we hunt for stolen base production to combat the category scarcity that defines our 5x5 strategy. **Luis Arraez** and **Matt Chapman** also offer high-floor production, with both hitters benefiting from wind blowing out at their respective parks, further elevating their daily efficiency scores well into the mid-60s.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision landed on **Taylor Ward**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 45.20. While **Taylor Ward** offers strong upside, the optimizer penalized him significantly due to a difficult matchup against George Kirby\u2014an elite arm with a 3.60 xERA\u2014and a park factor penalty that neutralized his projected output. We have opted to prioritize the platoon and park-advantage matchups provided by **Lawrence Butler** and **Drew Gilbert** instead. We are keeping a close watch on the status of **Cal Raleigh**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Tyler Freeman**, as their inclusion remains contingent on \"Lineup Pending\" status; any late-afternoon shifts in their batting order could necessitate a pivot to our bench depth, specifically checking for signs that **Brendan Donovan** or **Gleyber Torres** might be better suited if defensive substitutions or rest days impact our core. Keep in mind that with **Will Smith** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** sidelined on the IL, our roster flexibility is strained, making these daily efficiency metrics vital for protecting our remaining game caps.",
